# Auth & Tenancy Rules

See ADR-0009 and ADR-0010.

## Import boundaries

- `better-auth` is imported ONLY from `lib/auth/server.ts` (server) and
  `lib/auth/client.ts` (browser). Nowhere else.
- Authenticated API routes MUST call `resolveWorkspaceContext()` from
  `lib/auth/session.ts` — not ad-hoc session reads.
- `lib/aig/*` and `lib/arcade/*` MUST NOT import `lib/auth/*`.

## Tenancy model

- **Organization** — Better Auth `organization` plugin (company tenant).
- **Workspace** — AIG `workspaces` table (`production` | `sandbox`) scoped to org.
- **Default bootstrap** — `lib/auth/provision.ts` creates org + production workspace
  on first sign-in.

## Session vs Arcade identity

| Layer | Identity | Purpose |
| ----- | -------- | ------- |
| AIG sign-in | Better Auth user id + email | App access, audit, approver |
| Arcade OAuth | `user:{userId}` or `workspace:{workspaceId}` | Tool authorization + execute |

These are intentionally separate. Never conflate them.

## E2E / dev bypass

- `E2E_SKIP_AUTH=1` — anonymous workspace context for Playwright (see ADR-0009).
- Magic links without `RESEND_API_KEY` log to console in development only.
